(4650819, 671424, 15407, '<td valign="top">Hmmmm Very Well done... I would love to see a version with the colors switched ! I had an Old Gold $10 gold piece that had been burried in the ground and was severly pitted that i couldn''t enter because i could NOT get the coloring correct... The pitting (etching) left the coin with a degree of angular reflection that produced the entire visable coloe spectrum... and was not suitable for submission.  It looked as though it had been completely over processed. Youhave done a FINE job of capturing a wondeful rendition of the color "GOLD"! 8</td>', 'Hmmmm Very Well done... I would love to see a version with the colors switched ! I had an Old Gold $10 gold piece that had been burried in the ground and was severly pitted that i couldn''t enter because i could NOT get the coloring correct... The pitting (etching) left the coin with a degree of angular reflection that produced the entire visable coloe spectrum... and was not suitable for submission.  It looked as though it had been completely over processed. Youhave done a FINE job of capturing a wondeful rendition of the color "GOLD"! 8', '2008-04-21 02:31:18.000000', NULL, 1),
