(4849936, 670573, 41337, '<td valign="top">I assume this is a microwaved CD? I don''t think I''ve seen one that bubbled up like that before so from a curiosity standpoint it''s pretty cool. So good job adding a new spin on it. One thing I noticed when I messed around with this concept a while back was when I used a cd with an all black print on one side after it was cooked you could shine a light from underneath it would produce a very contrasty b/w look. You may want to try that if you haven''t already.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-07-29 19:35:53.</i></td>', 'I assume this is a microwaved CD? I don''t think I''ve seen one that bubbled up like that before so from a curiosity standpoint it''s pretty cool. So good job adding a new spin on it. One thing I noticed when I messed around with this concept a while back was when I used a cd with an all black print on one side after it was cooked you could shine a light from underneath it would produce a very contrasty b/w look. You may want to try that if you haven''t already.', '2008-07-29 20:34:18.000000', '2008-07-29 20:35:53.000000', 0),
